Subject: [PATCH 11/14] fix(trace): Smooth and Sharp say what they do
 differently (ADR-396)

The Smooth and Sharp descriptions in Trace Image, and the tutorial step
that suggests them, now name what these presets change rather than a
curve style they did not deliver. Smooth: for scans and noisy artwork;
sets its threshold from the image and removes isolated noise dots when
the image has many. Sharp: for pixel art and technical drawings; sets its
threshold from the image, keeps single-pixel marks and tiny holes, and
rounds fewer corners into curves. The tutorial says to try Smooth for a
noisy scan, or Sharp to keep single-pixel marks and tiny holes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
